  "source": "simulator_check/cases/star_grant_and_boundary.json",
  "question": "Does a permissions boundary that doesn't allow the request limit a bucket policy that grants it to everyone (*)? The analyzer treats * as a direct grant, which a boundary doesn't limit: a judgment call.",
  "description": "\"*\" with an ArnEquals condition on aws:PrincipalArn. AWS: \"Permissions boundaries and session policies do not limit permissions granted using the aws:PrincipalArn condition key with a wildcard(*) in the Principal element, unless the identity-based policies contain an explicit deny.\"",
  "readings": {
    "ALLOW": "the boundary doesn't limit a grant to everyone, as the analyzer assumes",
    "IMPLICIT_DENY": "the boundary limits it"
  },
